<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Restoration Shamans</span></h2>Crafted items are for the most part no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Leatherworker, you can equip anything Leatherworkers craft. There are a few notable exceptions to this, the Engineer goggles and the Alchemist Trinket. There is also the Inscription Staff, which is bound to account.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79330/relic-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Relic of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Chi-Ji</span></a> is made with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=773/inscription">
<img alt="Inscription" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tradeskill01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscription</span></a> and is about as good for healers as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a>, but should be much cheaper as it has no competition from non-healer specializations but will still get created as much as Yu'lon due to the random nature of card generation.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> is also made through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=773/inscription">
<img alt="Inscription" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tradeskill01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscription</span></a> and is one of our best Trinkets early on. As it is predicted be <b>extremely expensive</b>, players without a massive budget are advised to look at other uses for their gold early on in Mists of Pandaria.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79335/inscribed-red-fan">
<img alt="Inscribed Red Fan" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_1h_pandariatradeskill_c_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Red Fan</span></a> is also made with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=773/inscription">
<img alt="Inscription" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tradeskill01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscription</span></a>, and is less important than the Trinkets, but still a good upgrade early on while your choices are limited.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85826/lifekeepers-robe">
<img alt="Lifekeeper's Robe" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_mail_raidshaman_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lifekeeper's Robe</span></a> is an item made with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a>. It sports good stats and two sockets, making it very powerful early on when it competes against blue gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85840/stormbreaker-chestguard">
<img alt="Stormbreaker Chestguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_mail_raidshaman_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stormbreaker Chestguard</span></a> is also made with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a>. As it is an item with Crit that competes for the same spot as Tier pieces, it is not recommended to go for this one once we have access to Tier pieces from Celestial Dungeons.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85821/fists-of-lightning">
<img alt="Fists of Lightning" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_mail_raidshaman_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fists of Lightning</span></a> is also made with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a>. It has a good distribution of secondary stats, it does however compete against Tier pieces which makes it hard to slot into our gear set once Celestial Dungeons are available.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77537/energized-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Energized Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Energized Retinal Armor</span></a> is exclusive to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=202/engineering">
<img alt="Engineering" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a>. You can choose your two preferred secondary stats for this item, making it always be a strong pick before Tier sets are available.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> is exclusive to Alchemists and is very strong despite its low item level. You can use it until you have access to Celestial, raid Trinkets, or Inscription trinkets.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79340/inscribed-crane-staff">
<img alt="Inscribed Crane Staff" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_2h_pandariatradeskill_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Crane Staff</span></a> is made through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=773/inscription">
<img alt="Inscription" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tradeskill01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscription</span></a>, and is bound to account. This means you can craft it on an alt and send it to your main, although you can not buy it from other players. This also gives you the opportunity to send it between multiple characters with just one craft.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Restoration Shaman Trinkets</span></h2>You mostly want as many stats as possible from healing Trinkets, especially Intellect and Spirit which are plentiful in many. Generally speaking pick the highest listed item for the best effect, and make sure to use active Trinkets along with your cooldowns, for maximum effect.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Passive trinkets are generally superior for Restoration because they offer more stats for the same item level, but <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89081/blossom-of-pure-snow">
<img alt="Blossom of Pure Snow" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_herbd.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blossom of Pure Snow</span></a> is also a decent option as you will be farming the reputation for it regardless due to the other epic items being pre-raid best in slot and its effect is strong when combined with Restoration's many healing cooldowns.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79330/relic-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Relic of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Chi-Ji</span></a> is very strong and much cheaper than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a>, making it the favored Trinket for most players.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> is a very powerful Trinket. With a lot of Intellect and a strong Intellect proc with high uptime, this Trinket is far stronger than its item level would suggest.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86885/spirits-of-the-sun">
<img alt="Spirits of the Sun" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_29_sunkissedwine.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spirits of the Sun</span></a> is also a very powerful trinket, and the recommended one alongside a Darkmoon Card trinket.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86907/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a> provides a lot of Intellect and burst Haste, which can be strong for Mana regeneration with <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=41536/glyph-of-telluric-currents">
<img alt="Glyph of Telluric Currents" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glyph_majorshaman.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Telluric Currents</span></a> or for extra healing if it procs at the right time.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> has a very strong proc, allowing it to compete as one of our best pre-raid Trinkets.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81133/empty-fruit-barrel">
<img alt="Empty Fruit Barrel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cask_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Empty Fruit Barrel</span></a> this is a strong early trinket and also relatively easy to obtain.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86805/qin-xis-polarizing-seal">
<img alt="Qin-xi's Polarizing Seal" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trinketpanda_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qin-xi's Polarizing Seal</span></a> is similar to the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81133/empty-fruit-barrel">
<img alt="Empty Fruit Barrel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cask_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Empty Fruit Barrel</span></a> with slightly increased item level.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89081/blossom-of-pure-snow">
<img alt="Blossom of Pure Snow" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_herbd.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blossom of Pure Snow</span></a> is strong for Restoration, as you can line its on use effect with your cooldowns while also spreading them to hit various incoming damage events every minute.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89080/scroll-of-revered-ancestors">
<img alt="Scroll of Revered Ancestors" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_highborne_scroll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Scroll of Revered Ancestors</span></a> provides Spirit on use for a little bit of added Regen, which unfortunately does not multiply with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=16190/mana-tide-totem">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_summonwaterelemental.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mana Tide Totem</span></a>, making it a decent but not great option.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Restoration Shamans</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria the Spell Hit cap is 15% but Restoration Shamans do not have to worry about it because the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=112858/spiritual-insight">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_elementalabsorption.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spiritual Insight</span></a> passive takes care of all Spell Hit needs by default.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Gems for Restoration Shamans</span></h3>Gems are a great place to stack more of your favorite stats, which for Restoration tends to be Intellect, Haste and Spirit, since it is the only useful throughput stat that can appear on Blue Sockets.<br/>
<br/>You will generally want to take all socket bonuses as in Mists of Pandaria you get double the secondary stats for every point of Intellect on gems, making it worthwhile to not always go for pure Intellect.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76885/burning-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Burning Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Burning Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76694/brilliant-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76668/reckless-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Reckless Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reckless Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c9">Purple Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76686/purified-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Purified Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Imperial Amethyst</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c3">Engineering Gems</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77542/quick-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Quick Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Tinker's Gear</span></a> &amp; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77541/smooth-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Smooth Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Smooth Tinker's Gear</span></a></div></li></ul>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<hr/>Our restoration shaman guides are always updated with the latest information from in-game experience, simulations, and logs; make sure to check our changelog to this page, by clicking on <b>View Changelog</b> at the top of the page.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<hr/>
<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="feedback">Feedback</h2>Thanks for reading our class guides! If you have any feedback about the guides, feel free to leave a comment in the section below and we will reply as quickly as possible. If you'd like to talk with any of our writers directly you can do so by joining our <a href="http://discord.gg/wowhead" target="_blank">Discord Server</a> and finding them there!<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<br/>
<div class="pad exclude-units last"></div></div>